# oracle: kspace_style ewald/disp 1e-5 with Coulomb and dispersion long (pair lj/long/coul/long long long) and the automatic G-ewald (from the Coulomb estimate; the dispersion uses the same g), arithmetic mixing (7 structure factors), the default dispersion table, per-atom energy and virial summed, NVE 30 steps.
# oracle-inputs: w16disp_fcc2.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.0e-9, atoms 1.4e-9. The 1e-9 is the real-space Coulomb term of the core pair (its 12-bit erfc table emulation): elong and the per-atom k-space sums agree to 1e-15 at step 0.
units           lj
atom_style      charge
read_data       w16disp_fcc2.data
pair_style      lj/long/coul/long long long 2.5
pair_modify     mix arithmetic
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 0.5 1.1
kspace_style    ewald/disp 1.0e-5
compute         pea all pe/atom kspace
compute         sa all stress/atom NULL kspace
compute         pes all reduce sum c_pea
compute         sas all reduce sum c_sa[1] c_sa[2] c_sa[3] c_sa[4] c_sa[5] c_sa[6]
timestep        0.005
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step temp pe evdwl elong ecoul press pxx pyy pzz pxy c_pes c_sas[1] c_sas[2] c_sas[3] c_sas[4] c_sas[5] c_sas[6]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             30
